<main id="content" class="site-main post mt-article"><div class="page-header"><h1 class="entry-title">The Journey from Ancient Water Fountains to Modern Bubble Panels</h1></div><div class="page-content"><p class="mt-article-meta"><time datetime="2021-02-15T12:59:47">February 15, 2021</time></p><figure class="mt-article-hero"><img src="/wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg.avif" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg-100x100.avif 100w, /wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg-50x50.avif 50w, /wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg.avif 768w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px" width="768" height="360" alt="The Journey from Ancient Water Fountains to Modern Bubble Panels" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure><div class="mt-article-body"><p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="75579" data-permalink="https://www.midwest-tropical.com/the-journey-from-ancient-water-fountains-to-modern-bubble-panels-3/" data-orig-file="/wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg.avif" data-orig-size="768,360" data-comments-opened="0" data-image-title="The Journey from Ancient Water Fountains to Modern Bubble Panels" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="/wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels-jpg.avif" crossorigin="anonymous" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-75579" src="/wp-content/uploads/The-Journey-from-Ancient-Water-Fountains-to-Modern-Bubble-Panels1.jpg" alt="The Journey from Ancient Water Fountains to Modern Bubble Panels" width="1024" height="480" title=""></p>
<p>You&#x2122;d likely have a hard time recognizing the first-ever water fountain if you traveled back in time to observe it. Midwest Tropical, with its variety of technologically advanced water features, prides itself on being in touch with the roots and brings forth the best possible version of this modern marvel. Water wall designs that are available today have come a long way from what was the earliest known fountain carved from stone; it held precious drinking, ceremonial and religious water known to hail from around 200BC.</p>
<p>Gravity was the only source that drove the fountains in those days since they were situated along streams and rivers to supply drinking water. It wasn&#x2122;t until 6 BC that the ancient Romans began using water features as decorative pieces made into bronze stone masks of local and mythical heroes and animals. The Romans had a comprehensive aqueduct system that carried water for the several fountains installed throughout the city.</p>
<p><em>Rome had been named the ?city of fountains&#x2122; by 98AD, having created 591 public basins and 39 monumental fountains. </em></p>
<p><strong>The Middle Ages </strong></p>
<p>Fountains fell out of favor in the middle ages and were restricted to literature and art, gardens on the palace ground, and monasteries. These fountains were seen as symbols of purity, wisdom, life and innocence. These symbols often inspire water wall designs since they offer a glimpse into an era that has fascinated many authors and poets. If the writer in you needs inspiration, then this is the type of indoor tabletop fountain that will fit perfectly in your office space when waiting for inspiration to strike.</p>
<p>This was the time when these fountains were used to stimulate the onlookers and entertain passersby with playful sprays.</p>
<p><strong>The Baroque Eras </strong></p>
<p>Fountains underwent a massive transformation during the renaissance, where they become larger, complex, and grand. During this time, fountains were used to portray royalty and were seen as a symbol of wealth and power.</p>
<p>The many fountains still standing in Europe were built during this period. Apart from being regal tributes, they were also used for fun and theater. The many fountains found in the gardens were customized to spray water and play relaxing music.</p>
<p>The Baroque era witnessed a revival of the fountains as the old aqueducts of Ancient Rome was rebuilt and restored, providing unhindered water flow to the fountains. If present-day water wall designs seem like a reflection of ancient times, then this is the reason. From drinking sources to decoration to entertainment, water features have gone a tremendous change, which brings us to the modern-day.</p>
<p><strong>Modern-day Water Features</strong></p>
<p>Saying that the function and style of water features have evolved over the centuries would be an understatement. Nowhere near the technology what it is today, the ancient water feature boasting unique architecture couldn&#x2122;t hold a candle to what they have become today.</p>
<p>Today fountains are not just limited to gardens and parks but have now become a staple feature in indoor decor. They offer a multi-purpose existence that can create subtle style; make bold statements, and enhance the visual aesthetic of any commercial property.</p>
<p>There&#x2122;s no saying where the water features will end up in the next few centuries, but if you wish to use one now, head over to Midwest Tropical. You can find one that suits your needs, from rain walls to customized bubble panels. Become a part of history and choose a water feature to tie together your entire interior decoration theme.</p>
</div></div></main>

